# 29-nlogn-block-construction.patch  [FIND PRIOR PATCH FIRST]
#   Make CreateNewBlock self-sufficient: do local ancestor fee-rate tracking
#   inside the block assembler rather than reading pre-computed values from
#   mapTx. One pass over mempool candidates, maintaining a local map of
#   {txid → accumulated_ancestor_fee, accumulated_ancestor_size}, updated
#   as each tx is selected. Gives correct CPFP ordering without touching
#   mempool accounting at all.
#   This is step 1 of a 3-step sequence:
#     1. (this patch) Mining no longer depends on mempool CPFP accounting.
#     2. (patch 30) Remove mempool ancestor/descendant bookkeeping
#        (UpdateAncestorsOf, UpdateEntryForAncestors, CalculateDescendants, etc.)
#        and drop MEMPOOL_ANCESTOR_LIMIT / MEMPOOL_DESCENDANT_LIMIT caps.
#        Eviction strategy needs review: currently evicts by descendant fee
#        which requires the same accounting — needs a replacement policy
#        (e.g. evict by individual fee rate once package accounting is gone).
#     3. (patch 31) Cleanup: removeForBlock simplification, mempool lock
#        contention reduction, etc.
#   NOTE: Shammah wrote an earlier version of this patch (~2019, Bitcoin ABC
#   fork). Locate and port before writing from scratch.
#   eCash and BCH removed the chain limit but did NOT fix the O(n²) mining
#   construction — upstreaming step 1 alone would be a genuine improvement.
#
